				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Emmitt has great power, and the dude played through some pain, no doubt about that. However, I disagree to say Sanders couldnt have done well with a line the Cowboys had. I can't tell you how many times I saw Emmitt run up the middle without gettting a hand on him... he had holes opened up for him that you could drive a tank through.  Sanders was a slashing type back, but he still would have taken full advantage of holes like that. 
<br />

<br />
I like Emmitt, because the dude is tough as nails, but I dont think he was  a  Hall of Famer. He had a great line, and I often saw him getting run down and talked by linebackers. He was tough and had great power(I did see him plow right over a few 300+lb linemen), but he would never have gotten the numbers he got if it weren't for that offensive line.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
