			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Perhaps I didn't make my "opinion" of Emmitt Smith clear. Let me re-iterate... this is just my opinion of his talents. I realize the numbers he's put up, and where he sits in the stat books and history books, as well as his place in Canton. I dont think stats clearly reflects a players ability however. His numbers put him as one of the greatest running backs in the NFL. And I just dont think he was. &lt;shrugs&gt; And I personally don't even put him in the same league of other RBs in the Hall of Fame. 
<br />

<br />
I guess my measurement isn't really numbers.... it's watching them vs other great players. For example, not only have I seen  Barry Sanders make great runs, but more importantly make great defenders look bad... names like Cornelius Bennet, Rod Woodson, and Mike Singletary just flat out look silly... I've personally never seen Emmitt do that. &lt;shrugs&gt;
<br />

<br />
Again, just my opinion. He's tough as nails, and that's why the man has over 4,000 carries, which no other RB comes close to matching.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
